# Level 8 → 9 — Finding the Unique Line with sort and uniq

## Level Goal
Find the only line of text in `data.txt` that occurs exactly once.

## Description
The file contains many repeated lines. This level introduces the Unix pipeline pattern — chaining commands so the output of one feeds the input of the next.

## Approach
The solution required two commands chained together:

```bash
sort data.txt | uniq -u
```

`sort` arranges all lines alphabetically so duplicates become adjacent. `uniq -u` then prints only lines that appear exactly once.

